      "name": "bash",
      "arguments": "{\"command\":\"cat > /workspace/src/component.py <<'PY'\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Utilities for counting proper colorings of a labeled circle.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n_MODULUS = 998244353\\n\\n\\ndef count_valid_colorings(n: int, m: int) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Count assignments in which neighboring people have different colors.\\n\\n    The people are labeled, so rotations are distinct assignments. The first\\n    and last people are neighbors. The result is returned modulo 998244353.\\n\\n    Args:\\n        n: Number of people in the circle (2 <= n <= 10**6).\\n        m: Number of available colors (2 <= m <= 10**6).\\n\\n    Returns:\\n        The number of valid assignments modulo 998244353.\\n\\n    The cycle coloring polynomial is (m - 1)**n + (-1)**n * (m - 1).\\n    This also gives m * (m - 1) for n = 2, where the adjacency condition\\n    simply requires the two people to have different colors. Modular\\n    exponentiation computes it in O(log n) time and O(1) auxiliary space.\\n\\n    >>> count_valid_colorings(3, 3)\\n    6\\n    >>> count_valid_colorings(4, 2)\\n    2\\n    >>> count_valid_colorings(987654, 456789)\\n    778634319\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    choices = m - 1\\n    correction = choices if n % 2 == 0 else -choices\\n    return (pow(choices, n, _MODULUS) + correction) % _MODULUS\\nPY\\ncd /workspace && python tests.py\"}",
      "status": "completed"
    }
